# Architecture (Frontend)

Multi-tenant SaaS Restaurant Management System. This is the Angular 20 frontend; the backend (ASP.NET Core 10 + EF Core + PostgreSQL) lives in a separate repo.

## Key principles
- Feature-based folders; SOLID; keep features modular.
- Build for future expansion without breaking existing features.
- Communicate with the backend only through DTOs over the REST API.

## Multi-tenancy (critical)
- Every tenant is a restaurant; data is isolated per `RestaurantId` server-side.
- NEVER send `RestaurantId` from the client. The backend derives it from JWT claims.
- Store the JWT securely and attach it to every API request.

## Auth & registration
- Login form fields: Restaurant Name + Username + Password.
- NO public sign-up screen. Restaurants and users are created only by an admin (in-app), never via a public form.
- Roles: Admin, Manager, Cashier. Show/hide UI by permissions.

## Navigation groups
- **Sales:** Dashboard, POS, Categories, Menu Items, Sales Reports
- **Inventory:** UOMs, RM Categories, Raw Materials, Suppliers, Purchases, Purchase Reports, Stock Report
- **Admin:** Users, Roles, Restaurant Settings, Restaurants (platform)

## Scope
Auth, Restaurant settings, Users, Roles, Categories, Menu, POS/Orders, Invoice printing, Sales Reports, Dashboard, Inventory (UOM, RM categories, raw materials + pack sizes, suppliers, purchases, stock), Purchase/Stock reports with Excel/PDF export. Kitchen, Recipe, Accounting, etc. remain future work.
